<BaseLayout title={'FAQ: working with The Aha Company'} description={'How an engagement with The Aha Company runs, for financial institutions putting regulated assets onchain, protocols expanding to Stellar, XRPL or Canton, and ecosystems that need developer tooling.'}>
<main class="faq_main"><div class="intro"><p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p><h1 class="intro_h1">Questions we hear before the first call.</h1><p class="text-lead">Answered from the engagements we have run. If yours is not here, ask it on the call.</p></div><div class="faq_layout"><nav aria-label="FAQ sections" class="faq_subnav"><a class="faq_pill" href="#working">Working with us</a><a class="faq_pill" href="#institutions">Financial institutions</a><a class="faq_pill" href="#protocols">Protocols and products</a><a class="faq_pill" href="#ecosystems">Ecosystems and foundations</a></nav><div class="faq_content"><section class="faq_group" id="working"><h2 class="faq_group-h2">Working with us</h2><div class="faq_list"><details class="faq_item"><summary class="faq_q"><div class="inline-text">What does The Aha Company do?</div><span aria-hidden="true" class="faq_icon">+</span></summary><p class="faq_answer">We are a blockchain integration partner. Three kinds of clients come to us: financial institutions putting regulated assets onchain, protocols and products expanding to a new network, and ecosystems and foundations that need developer tooling. The engineers who build the networks' tooling do the integrations.</p></details><details class="faq_item"><summary class="faq_q"><div class="inline-text">How does an engagement start?</div><span aria-hidden="true" class="faq_icon">+</span></summary><p class="faq_answer">With a working session, not a pitch. For an institution, a scoping session with your technical lead; for a protocol, an integration roadmap; for an ecosystem, a two-week DevX audit. Then an NDA and an MOU with the scope cut into milestones your team can verify.</p></details><details class="faq_item"><summary class="faq_q"><div class="inline-text">What are the ways to work with you?</div><span aria-hidden="true" class="faq_icon">+</span></summary><p class="faq_answer">Four. Integration partner: fixed scope, milestone-based, our team end to end. Architecture lead: we design the system and lead delivery with your engineers or your consultancy's. Embedded principal engineer: a senior engineer placed with your team for a quarter or more. Programs for ecosystems: DevX audits, tooling roadmaps, accelerator and hackathon mentoring.</p></details><details class="faq_item"><summary class="faq_q"><div class="inline-text">Who will we be talking to?</div><span aria-hidden="true" class="faq_icon">+</span></summary><p class="faq_answer">An engineer. The first call is thirty minutes with someone who has shipped the kind of system you are asking about, not a sales team.</p></details><details class="faq_item"><summary class="faq_q"><div class="inline-text">Where is the team based?</div><span aria-hidden="true" class="faq_icon">+</span></summary><p class="faq_answer" data-rv="faq-team">Twelve-plus engineers across the United States, Europe and Brazil, with entities in the United States, France and Brazil.</p></details><details class="faq_item"><summary class="faq_q"><div class="inline-text">Which networks do you work on?</div><span aria-hidden="true" class="faq_icon">+</span></summary><p class="faq_answer">Stellar, where we are core contributors, Stellar Community Fund reviewers and tooling maintainers. XRPL, as a Ripple program partner. Canton, where integrations are in progress. Ethereum as the EVM counterpart for cross-chain work.</p></details></div></section><section class="faq_group" id="institutions"><h2 class="faq_group-h2">Financial institutions</h2><div class="faq_list"><details class="faq_item"><summary class="faq_q"><div class="inline-text">Have you taken regulated assets to mainnet?</div><span aria-hidden="true" class="faq_icon">+</span></summary><p class="faq_answer" data-rv="faq-mainnet">Yes. EURCV, Société Générale FORGE's regulated euro stablecoin, runs on issuance and governance contracts we built, live on Stellar mainnet since Q1 2026 with €20M+ issued. We also architected an internal settlement stablecoin for a top US commercial bank, in a live pilot on Stellar, and we are building a tokenized share class of a money-market fund for a regulated European private bank.</p></details><details class="faq_item"><summary class="faq_q"><div class="inline-text">What compliance controls can the contracts enforce?</div><span aria-hidden="true" class="faq_icon">+</span></summary><p class="faq_answer">Role separation between admin, mint and burn authority; freeze and clawback; allow and deny lists; alerting-to-freeze automation; mint and burn bridges to your core banking. For fund units and deposits, transfer restrictions live in the contract, with subscriptions and redemptions onchain.</p></details><details class="faq_item"><summary class="faq_q"><div class="inline-text">How do you handle custody and keys?</div><span aria-hidden="true" class="faq_icon">+</span></summary><p class="faq_answer">Custodian and MPC integrations, KYT through the custodian, smart accounts and passkeys. Who holds which key is settled in the scoping session, before any code is written.</p></details><details class="faq_item"><summary class="faq_q"><div class="inline-text">What happens after mainnet?</div><span aria-hidden="true" class="faq_icon">+</span></summary><p class="faq_answer">Production surfaces questions a testnet never asks. Deployment comes with runbooks and handover, and we keep evolving the system with your team after launch.</p></details><details class="faq_item"><summary class="faq_q"><div class="inline-text">Can you work inside our team, or with our consultancy?</div><span aria-hidden="true" class="faq_icon">+</span></summary><p class="faq_answer" data-rv="faq-pwc">Yes. In the architecture-lead model we design the system and lead delivery with your engineers or your consultancy's. We have a co-selling alliance with PwC US to tackle clients together.</p></details></div></section><section class="faq_group" id="protocols"><h2 class="faq_group-h2">Protocols and products</h2><div class="faq_list"><details class="faq_item"><summary class="faq_q"><div class="inline-text">What does integrating onto a new network involve?</div><span aria-hidden="true" class="faq_icon">+</span></summary><p class="faq_answer">An integration roadmap that maps your surface to the target network, then native contracts, adapters and SDKs, routing and liquidity, matched to the guarantees you already give users and tested against your existing suite.</p></details><details class="faq_item"><summary class="faq_q"><div class="inline-text">Have you done this before?</div><span aria-hidden="true" class="faq_icon">+</span></summary><p class="faq_answer">LI.FI's Stellar integration runs on Soroban contracts we built, extending its cross-chain reach.</p></details><details class="faq_item"><summary class="faq_q"><div class="inline-text">Can the integration be funded?</div><span aria-hidden="true" class="faq_icon">+</span></summary><p class="faq_answer">Often. Where an ecosystem program applies, we scope and draft the application; where it doesn't, we say so.</p></details><details class="faq_item"><summary class="faq_q"><div class="inline-text">Who maintains the integration after launch?</div><span aria-hidden="true" class="faq_icon">+</span></summary><p class="faq_answer">Your engineers can. Launch comes with docs and a maintenance plan written for your team to run.</p></details></div></section><section class="faq_group" id="ecosystems"><h2 class="faq_group-h2">Ecosystems and foundations</h2><div class="faq_list"><details class="faq_item"><summary class="faq_q"><div class="inline-text">What is a DevX audit?</div><span aria-hidden="true" class="faq_icon">+</span></summary><p class="faq_answer">Two senior engineers spend two weeks on your real onboarding path, then deliver a tooling roadmap agreed with your engineering team: CLIs, scaffolding, registries, sandboxes, wallets.</p></details><details class="faq_item"><summary class="faq_q"><div class="inline-text">What have you built for ecosystems?</div><span aria-hidden="true" class="faq_icon">+</span></summary><p class="faq_answer" data-rv="faq-ecosystems">For Stellar: core contributions to the Stellar CLI, Scaffold Stellar, the Stellar Registry, Nido (our open-source passkey wallet) and Perch, its policy layer, Moonlight (a privacy layer for payments) and Tansu (onchain governance and release records). For XRPL: GhostSig, a passkey wallet for XRPL and Stellar, and accelerator cohorts and hackathons with Ripple, mentoring teams from prototype to go live.</p></details><details class="faq_item"><summary class="faq_q"><div class="inline-text">Is the tooling open source?</div><span aria-hidden="true" class="faq_icon">+</span></summary><div class="faq_answer" data-rv="faq-os"><div class="inline-text">Yes. Scaffold Stellar, the Stellar Registry and Tansu are maintained as public goods, with a quarterly proposal and review. Each tool, where its code lives, its status and its audits are on our </div><a class="faq_answer-link" href="/open-source">open-source page</a><div class="inline-text">.</div></div></details><details class="faq_item"><summary class="faq_q"><div class="inline-text">Can you place an engineer with our team?</div><span aria-hidden="true" class="faq_icon">+</span></summary><p class="faq_answer">Yes, a principal engineer for a quarter or more, as with the Stellar Development Foundation.</p></details></div></section></div></div></main>
<Cta heading={'Still have a question? Ask an engineer.'} />
</BaseLayout>
